sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Code-to-model traceability: 72/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "Most modelling functions carry a docstring citing a specific equation, section or figure (local W_n -> Eq. 3.12, lateral W_n^lat(q) -> Eq. 4.9, eigenfunction -> §4.2 Eqs. 4.14-4.16, cubic equations -> Eqs. 5.9-5.15 and Figs. 37-40, map -> §2 / 2002 Eq. 1.1, tangent map -> 2002 §1.1), and the section banners and panel titles name the figures being reproduced. Deductions: planform_modes hard-codes per-mode phase multipliers (0.35, -0.25) and an amplitude of -1 on one hex_pi mode with no citation, and that hex_pi is cos k1 - cos k2 + cos k3 rather than the paper's H_pi (-8); tanh sharpness, the m <= 4 truncation and the +/-1.5 clamp are traced to upstream planform.rs, not to any paper step (-4); lateral_spread_factor and modified_bessel_i have no equation citation (-3); the even-branch hex stability condition (gamma_hex > 0 and gamma0 + 4 gamma_hex > 0, skipping 2 gamma_hex < gamma0) is uncited (-4); the Lyapunov tie-break is acknowledged as heuristic but is still what decides SELECTED vs STABLE-coexisting (-3); the 'Eq.' numbers for W_n could not be verified and read as approximate (-2); the ledger panel and CSV columns documenting what each number means are credited. Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L519–L532: local_weight_coeff cites Eq. 3.12; lateral_spread_factor has no citation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L519-L532>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L982–L1013: planform_modes: uncited phase multipliers 0.35 / -0.25 and hex_pi amplitude -1 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L982-L1013>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L722–L735: Normal form, Lyapunov functional and tie-break documented and flagged as heuristic <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L722-L735>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L797–L805: Even-branch hex stability condition skips 2 gamma_hex < gamma0 without a cited reason <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L797-L805>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.72"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Code-to-model traceability' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dct:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary) + Gemini 4 Argon (independent blinded second assessor)" .
}

